The product master should include product name, canonical SKU, channel-specific SKU, ASIN, Shopify product ID, Shopify variant ID, UPC, category, launch date, active/inactive status, COGS, selling price, breakeven ROAS, TACOS target, supplier, and subscription eligibility.
1.5 Source precedence and no double counting
Sales channel and marketing source are different. Amazon and TikTok Shop are sales channels. Meta and Google are marketing sources that normally drive Shopify Online Store orders.
For the requested Meta/TikTok Shop/Amazon graph, label Meta as “Shopify sales attributed to Meta.” Do not add all Shopify sales plus Meta-attributed Shopify sales, because that would double count the same orders.
The combined company total must come from deduplicated orders by order ID and sales channel.
Show platform-reported attribution and Shopify attribution in separate columns; never blend them into one unlabeled number.
