3. QuickBooks and Cash Runway
3.1 Cash burn definition must be approved by Patrick
The dashboard currently references a monthly budget of $484,001.80 and 39.8 weeks of runway with a GREEN status. Those figures should not be treated as final until Patrick defines the formula, accounts, exclusions, and forecast horizon.
Item
Required Definition
Available cash
Unrestricted operating cash that can actually pay obligations; exclude restricted balances and transfers between company accounts.
Operating cash burn
Trailing average cash operating outflows minus operating cash inflows. Patrick must define whether to use 4, 8, or 13 weeks.
Inventory cash commitments
Open PO deposits, balances due, freight, duties, and WSA/Amazon inbound costs must be shown separately or included in a committed-cash scenario.
Runway formula
Available cash divided by average weekly cash burn. If burn is zero or cash-positive, display “Cash-flow positive” rather than an infinite or invalid number.
Forecast runway
A 13-week cash forecast that includes known due dates is more useful than a simple trailing average for a company with large inventory payments.
Status bands
Patrick must approve GREEN/YELLOW/RED thresholds. The status may not be GREEN merely because a number exists.

Recommended display: Current Cash, Monthly Budget, Trailing 13-Week Average Burn, Known 13-Week Commitments, Basic Runway, Committed Runway, Data Through, and Patrick Confirmed date.
