13. Technical Reliability Requirements
Validate every JSON file against a schema before publishing. Reject malformed files rather than breaking the entire dashboard.
Write files atomically so the page never reads a partially written JSON file.
Add a post-run smoke test that loads the dashboard data and verifies required fields, dates, numeric types, and product coverage.
Record each source pull in a run log with start time, end time, records returned, status, and error message.
Keep the last known good file, but visibly label it STALE if the current run fails.
Never convert missing values to zero. Zero means the source confirmed zero; Missing means the source did not provide the value.
Use one product master and one channel/source mapping table rather than hard-coded product names in multiple scripts.
Provide an owner-facing error message. “Couldn’t load dashboard data” is not enough; identify the missing file, invalid field, authentication issue, or failed job.
14. Acceptance Criteria
The dashboard loads without a connectors_data.json error and every menu page renders.
No page displays null, undefined, NaN, unexplained dashes, or false zero values.
No page can be GREEN when a critical KPI is Missing, Stale, or Authentication Required.
Every displayed metric has a data-through date, last-refresh time, source, and status.
The five new products appear in every applicable product-level report without editing separate page code.
Morning Overview contains the DAAS channel graph, Reviews card, and bottom dropdown Source Status Board.
Shopify provides order/source/campaign/product reporting, new versus repeat customers, CAC, ROAS, and a source graph.
Amazon Last Week, Last Month, Ad Performance, S&S, Seller Central, Listing Analyzer, and Market Tracker contain data or a clear scheduled/pipeline status.
Product Reviews lists individual Amazon and Shopify reviews for the last 30 days.
Inventory Position is above Inventory Risk, followed by SKU Detail.
Amazon and Shopify subscription dashboards are separate; Business Health provides the combined summary.
Returns versus benchmark and Key Metrics versus Targets are populated by SKU/ASIN where applicable.
Google and Meta dashboards include the metrics and drilldowns defined in this report.
Will can understand why a value is missing without opening code, GitHub, or Slack.
15. Recommended Delivery Sequence
Phase
Work
1 — Data integrity
Fix connectors_data.json, schema validation, run logging, stale/missing states, timestamps, and false GREEN logic.
2 — Core operating pages
Morning Overview, QuickBooks, Shopify, Amazon missing sections, Product Reviews, and Inventory order.
3 — Business Health
Populate missing cards, S&S split/combined view, returns by SKU/ASIN, and metrics versus targets.
4 — Advertising dashboards
Complete Meta and Google campaign, creative, attribution, product, and alert reporting.
5 — Automation hardening
Move away from employee-specific browser dependence, document Will browser logins, and automate scheduled reports.
6 — QA and signoff
Run source-by-source tests, compare totals to platform reports, and obtain Patrick/Will approval on formulas and targets.

